Given, \(K_c=1.\) The open-loop transfer function is, \[G(s)=\frac{e^{-s}}{s+1}\] The steady-state error for a unit step input is, \[e_{ss}=\frac{1}{1+K_p}, \qquad \text{where }~~K_p=\lim_{s\to0}G(s)\] \[K_p
=
\lim_{s\to0}\frac{e^{-s}}{s+1}
=
1\] Therefore, \[e_{ss}
=
\frac{1}{1+1}
=
\frac12\] \[\boxed{(B)\;\dfrac12}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>For steady-state error analysis, the transport delay \(e^{-sT}\) is evaluated at \(s=0\), giving \(e^{-sT}=1.\) Hence the transport delay does not affect the steady-state error.</li></ul></div>
